WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.672
An unwritten language with a living literature.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.149
Most islanders speak Soqotri, one of the Modern South Arabian languages:

00:00:09.149 --> 00:00:11.358
a Semitic group distinct from Arabic.

00:00:11.358 --> 00:00:15.836
It has traditionally been unwritten, with a rich oral literature of poetry,

00:00:15.836 --> 00:00:17.807
proverbs and knowledge of plants.

00:00:18.907 --> 00:00:22.890
Traditional life combines herding in the mountains, fishing on the coast,

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.636
and date gardens in the valleys.

00:00:24.636 --> 00:00:26.382
Resource use was long regulated:

00:00:26.382 --> 00:00:31.021
nineteenth-century accounts describe dragon's blood land divided into lots and leased

00:00:31.021 --> 00:00:32.003
to herding groups.

00:00:33.103 --> 00:00:36.661
Today Socotra faces Baldacchino's question in its sharpest form.

00:00:36.661 --> 00:00:39.441
Rapid change is being decided far from the island,

00:00:39.441 --> 00:00:44.446
while the people with the deepest knowledge of its ecosystems have the least formal power.
